{"title":"42","section":"10250","heading":"Termination of Office","lead":"The Office shall cease to exist not later than 30 days after the date 7 years after December 22, 1987.","tree":[],"notes":[{"topic":"editorialNotes","text":"Editorial Notes"},{"topic":"codification","text":"Codification Pub. L. 100–202 and Pub. L. 100–203 added identical sections."},{"topic":"amendments","text":"Amendments1992—Pub. L. 102–486 substituted “7 years” for “5 years”."}],"sourceCredit":"(Pub. L. 97–425, title IV, § 410, as added Pub. L. 100–202, § 101(d) [title III], Dec. 22, 1987, 101 Stat. 1329–104, 1329–121; Pub. L. 100–203, title V, § 5041, Dec. 22, 1987, 101 Stat. 1330–247; amended Pub. L. 102–486, title VIII, § 802(a), Oct. 24, 1992, 106 Stat. 2923.)","releasePoint":"119-102","ancestors":[{"type":"title","num":"Title 42—","heading":"THE PUBLIC HEALTH AND WELFARE","identifier":"/us/usc/t42"},{"type":"chapter","num":"CHAPTER 108—","heading":"NUCLEAR WASTE POLICY","identifier":"/us/usc/t42/ch108"},{"type":"subchapter","num":"SUBCHAPTER IV—","heading":"NUCLEAR WASTE NEGOTIATOR","identifier":"/us/usc/t42/ch108/schIV"}]}